⦿ .spun — the five-fold spin of The Bhakti Refusal
node JTI · JTI · ⟦The Bhakti Refusal:JTI:28b8b9⟧

WHO   — The Bhakti Refusal — the saints who said no
WHAT  — Centuries of refusal: Ravidas imagined 'Begumpura,' a city without caste; Kabir mocked ritual hierarchy; Basava (12th c.) promoted inter-caste marriage and dining. Devotion to a god who sees no caste was, repeatedly, a weapon against it.
WHERE — JTI · the caste system  Framework inputs: the Rigveda, Manusmriti, Dumont, ancient-DNA genetics, Dirks, the Constitution, Pew/IHDS, Ambedkar  Conductor / external anchor: ROOT0 (catalogued into UD0)
WHY   — Because caste was always contested from within — the refusal is as Indian as the doctrine, and far older than the Constitution.
HOW   — By devotional poetry, casteless congregations, and the radical claim that love of the divine erases rank.

awareness — what the node knows of itself:
  Before the law said no, the saints did — Begumpura, the city with no caste and no sorrow, sung into being by a man they called untouchable.

